.TH PSVariance 3 2023-12-07 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSVariance

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSFloat  
.br
\fBPSVariance\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the statistical varicance of the elements of vector \fIa\fR having length defined by \fIlength\fR.
.br
The variance is the sum of the squared difference of the difference between each value of \fIa\fR and the mean value of \fIa\fR.
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The variance of vector \fIa\fR values or zero if \fIa\fR is \fINULL\fR.
